# The codes this pack must be refused with: by the charter service (scripts/ci/charter_service_check.py)
# and by pack-check (scripts/ci/charter_pack_check.py).
# pack_version is not a semantic (PEP 440) version. Every other file is the valid example pack's, under its own
# pack_id and name, so the version is the only fault. The pack-descriptor schema asks only for a non-empty string,
# so the per-pack schema pass accepts it. The service refuses it at composition (pack_unreadable) and at
# registration (validation_failed, its violation pack_version_invalid).
#
# pack-check `failed`: rc.3 crashes on it with exit 2 and no report (spec-kitty-charter#624). The gate treats
# exit 2 as a failure, never as a skip. Once #624 lands, pack-check reports the fault instead, `failed` no
# longer matches, and this line must name the code pack-check then gives (likely pack_version_invalid).
composition: pack_unreadable
registration: validation_failed
precheck: accepted
pack-check: failed
